  "notes": "Recommended Course Sequence for the Certificate of Achievement, published in the 2023-2024 catalog (p. 105), including a Summer term. CATALOG ARITHMETIC TYPO (kept verbatim, documented): the Summer term prints 'Total Number of Units: 10' but contains only the single 4-unit ATECH 24A; computed 4 makes the certificate total exactly the catalog's stated 50-unit minimum. Hard prerequisites from the degree requirements notes are coded and satisfied in sequence order: ATECH 24A requires ATECH 11; ATECH 14 requires ATECH 11 and ATECH 12; ATECH 27 requires ATECH 24A. ATECH 27 prerequisite discrepancy documented: the Engine Performance degree-requirements page states 'Atech 24A is a prerequisite for Atech 27', while the ATECH 27 course description (p. 127) lists 'Prerequisite: ATECH 21'. Both are coded; both are satisfied in-sequence. Revalidated 2026-10-01 against the official College of Alameda 2024-2025 catalog (CoA-Catalog-24-25_PRINT_v1.pdf, 7,590,937 bytes, 416 pages; live alameda.edu copy 404s, retrieved via Wayback Machine capture 20250808180750): recommended course sequence verified identical to the 2023-2024 transcription. The 2025-2026 catalog is published only on Curriqunet (JS-rendered, no downloadable PDF); revalidation against it is pending a live-browser pass.",
